        interviewDefinition: "An application design where no request-specific state (like session data) is stored in the memory of a particular instance, so any instance can serve any request.",
        whyItMatters: "It's what makes horizontal scaling simple — a load balancer can send each request to any healthy instance without worrying about where a user 'lives.'",
